<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liaoshen campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liaoshen campaign was the first of the three great campaigns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war">Chinese Civil War</a>, fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> from September to November 1948. Communist forces under Lin Biao took Jinzhou, cutting off the Nationalist armies in the north-east, and then captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changchun">Changchun</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shenyang">Shenyang</a>, destroying some 470,000 Nationalist troops and giving the Communists control of Manchuria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liaoshen-campaign.jpg" alt="Liaoshen campaign" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Final_Attack_on_Jinzhou.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
